A destroy clears the table slot of a process only when the process dies with it.
A process whose table went with another pool keeps naming the freed table;
a process's table slot is empty or names a live table.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: process's table slot names no live table

